msgstr "file read、argument handling、JSON rendering、exit status を pure frontend から隔離します。"

#: manual/design/cli/gda_expr_cli.md:21
msgid "Keeping transport separate makes parser tests deterministic, at the cost of a small adapter API used only by the main CLI."
msgstr "transport 分離で parser test は deterministic になりますが、main CLI 専用の小さな adapter API が残ります。"

#: manual/design/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:1
msgid "`cli/itl_expr_cli` Design"
msgstr "`cli/itl_expr_cli` 設計"

#: manual/design/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:9
msgid "It reads ITL files, applies optional operation filters, delegates cases to `frontend/itl_expr`, and renders stable summaries."
msgstr "ITL file を読み、optional operation filter を適用し、case を `frontend/itl_expr` に委譲して stable summary を出力します。"

#: manual/design/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:13
msgid "Unsupported cases remain explicit; strict mode changes gate success, not the underlying case disposition."
msgstr "unsupported case は明示したままです。strict mode は gate success だけを変更し、case disposition は書き換えません。"

#: manual/design/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:17
msgid "Filesystem access and output are effects; interval parsing and arithmetic remain pure package calls."
msgstr "filesystem access と output が effect で、interval parse と arithmetic は pure package call のままです。"

#: manual/design/cli/itl_expr_cli.md:21
msgid "The adapter avoids duplicating interval semantics but intentionally leaves phase planning to Python tooling."
msgstr "interval semantics の重複を避ける一方、phase planning は Python tooling に委ねます。"

#: manual/design/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:1
msgid "`cli/mpfr_expr_cli` Design"
msgstr "`cli/mpfr_expr_cli` 設計"

#: manual/design/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:9
msgid "It identifies sqrt versus integer-power input, delegates parsing and execution, and renders one-file summaries."
msgstr "sqrt と integer-power input を識別し、parse/execution を委譲して single-file summary を出力します。"

#: manual/design/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:13
msgid "Grammar selection is transport metadata, not a numerical heuristic; unsupported files fail before execution."
msgstr "grammar selection は transport metadata であり数値 heuristic ではありません。unsupported file は実行前に失敗します。"

#: manual/design/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:17
msgid "File reads and rendering are effects. MPFR-format parsing and binary comparison remain in `frontend/mpfr_expr`."
msgstr "file read と rendering が effect で、MPFR format parse と binary comparison は `frontend/mpfr_expr` に残ります。"

#: manual/design/cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md:21
msgid "Automatic grammar selection keeps commands short but is intentionally limited to repository-pinned formats."
msgstr "自動 grammar 選択で command は短くなりますが、repository-pinned format だけを対象にします。"

#: manual/design/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:1
msgid "`cli/testfloat_expr_cli` Design"
msgstr "`cli/testfloat_expr_cli` 設計"

#: manual/design/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:9
msgid "It validates function, rounding, tininess, and shard options, then delegates parsing and execution to `frontend/testfloat_expr`."
msgstr "function、rounding、tininess、shard option を検証し、parse/execution を `frontend/testfloat_expr` に委譲します。"

#: manual/design/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:13
msgid "Metadata is explicit and never inferred from filenames; JSON fields and exit status remain stable for tooling."
msgstr "metadata は明示し、filename から推測しません。JSON field と exit status は tooling 向けに安定させます。"

#: manual/design/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:17
msgid "File access, option parsing, rendering, and exit status are effects isolated at this edge."
msgstr "file access、option parsing、rendering、exit status をこの edge に隔離します。"

#: manual/design/cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md:21
msgid "Explicit metadata is more verbose but prevents a wrong format or rounding policy from silently selecting another oracle contract."
msgstr "明示 metadata は冗長ですが、誤った format/rounding policy が別 oracle contract を黙って選ぶことを防ぎます。"

#: manual/design/consistency.md:1
msgid "`consistency` Design"
msgstr "`consistency` 設計"

#: manual/design/consistency.md:9
msgid "Tests compare aliases, capability traits, checked wrappers, semantic projections, and migration invariants across numeric packages."
msgstr "numeric package 間の alias、capability trait、checked wrapper、semantic projection、migration invariant を比較します。"

#: manual/design/consistency.md:13
msgid "Every witness is small and deterministic; external corpus completeness belongs to conformance runners."
msgstr "witness は小さく deterministic です。external corpus completeness は conformance runner が担当します。"

#: manual/design/consistency.md:17
msgid "The package has no runtime API or IO. Failures are test assertions identifying a contract mismatch."
msgstr "runtime API と IO はなく、failure は contract mismatch を示す test assertion です。"

#: manual/design/consistency.md:21
msgid "Centralizing cross-package laws catches drift, while package-local algorithm details remain in their owning white-box tests."
msgstr "cross-package law を集中すると drift を検出できますが、package-local algorithm detail は所有 package の white-box test に残します。"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:1
msgid "`decimal` Design"
msgstr "`decimal` 設計"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:3
msgid "`decimal` is the IEEE-oriented arbitrary-precision decimal core of `floating` 0.8.0. It combines a quantum-preserving decimal value, explicit contextual rounding and flags, decimal32/64/128 interchange, and certified elementary functions. The separate [`decimal_gda`](decimal_gda.md) package owns sticky General Decimal Arithmetic status and traps; the two value types are intentionally not aliases."
msgstr "`decimal` は 0.8.0 の IEEE-oriented arbitrary-precision decimal core です。Quantum-preserving value、explicit context/flags、decimal32/64/128 interchange、certified elementary を提供します。 [`decimal_gda`](decimal_gda.md) は独立 GDA sticky/trap model で、型は alias ではありません。"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:12
msgid "The implementation is organized around one semantic rule: coefficient kernels compute exact integer facts, while a shared finalization step alone decides the bounded decimal result. This gives the following pipeline:"
msgstr "Coefficient kernel は exact integer facts のみを計算し、shared finalization が bounded decimal result を決定します：classification → exact sign/coefficient/preferred exponent → one rounding → exponent/subnormal/tininess/clamp → value + flags。Kernel optimization は quantum/signed zero/NaN/ flags を変えません。"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:25
msgid "Consequently, a faster multiplication or division algorithm cannot alter rounding, quantum, signed zero, NaN payloads, or flags. These observable states are owned by the decimal layer, not by the coefficient representation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal.md:29
msgid "Representation And Cohorts"
msgstr "Representation / Cohort"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:31
msgid "A finite `Decimal` stores an independent sign, non-negative coefficient, base-10 exponent, precision, and special-value state. Its mathematical value is"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal.md:38
#, fuzzy
msgid "The same number may have several cohort representations. For example, `1.2300` has quantum `-4`, whereas `1.23` has quantum `-2`. Parsing preserves the input exponent when it fits the requested precision; `normalized()` or `reduce_ctx()` removes removable powers of ten only when the caller explicitly requests canonical cohort form. Numeric comparison and `compare_total` are therefore different relations."
msgstr "Finite value は `(-1)^negative × coefficient × 10^exponent10`。`1.2300` (quantum -4) と `1.23` (-2) は同じ数値でも別 cohort です。Precision に収まる parse は input exponent を保持し、 `normalized/reduce_ctx` の明示呼出だけが 10 の factor を除きます。"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:45
msgid "The private `DecCoeff` uses an inline representation for small magnitudes and canonical little-endian base-`10^9` `UInt` limbs for larger values. Limb arrays have no leading zero and carry an exact decimal digit count. `BigInt` remains at public conversion/serialization boundaries and in test oracles, but decimal hot paths operate on `DecCoeff`."
msgstr "Private `DecCoeff` は small inline または canonical little-endian base-`10^9` limbs + exact digit count。`BigInt` は public conversion/serialization と oracle boundary に限定します。"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:51
msgid "IEEE 754 Alignment"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal.md:53
msgid "`DecimalContext::ieee754()` and decimal32/64/128 presets make precision, rounding, exponent limits, clamp, and before/after-rounding tininess explicit. Context operations return `(Decimal, DecimalFlags)`; there is no ambient rounding mode or process-global flag register. FMA preserves the exact product through aligned addition and performs one final rounding."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal.md:59
#, fuzzy
msgid "`DecimalInterchange` implements both DPD and BID encodings for decimal32, decimal64, and decimal128. Decode and encode preserve signed zero, infinity, quiet/signaling NaN, and payload state. Non-canonical finite encodings are handled at this encoding boundary rather than leaking bit-layout rules into ordinary arithmetic."
msgstr "IEEE context/preset は precision、rounding、exponent、clamp、tininess を明示し、`*_ctx` は tuple を返します。FMA は exact product を aligned addition まで保持し一回 rounding。 `DecimalInterchange` は DPD/BID と signed zero/infinity/qNaN/sNaN/payload を扱います。 GDA sticky/trap behavior は `decimal_gda` の責務です。"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:65
msgid "The checked IEEE matrix covers the operation/encoding rows declared in `testdata/decimal/ieee/conformance_matrix.json`. GDA-compatible operations that remain on `Decimal` are compatibility surface, not evidence that this package threads GDA traps. Applications requiring sticky status, fixed trap precedence, or `.decTest` behavior must use `decimal_gda`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal.md:73
msgid "The selector considers limb count, density, balance ratio, square shape, transform length, and target. Sparse coefficients use compressed nonzero products; strongly unbalanced coefficients are divided into balanced blocks. Dense balanced multiplication follows schoolbook/Comba, Karatsuba, Toom-3, and dual-modulus NTT stages."
msgstr "Selector は limb count、density、balance、square、transform length、target を使用し、dense balanced は schoolbook/Comba→Karatsuba→Toom-3→dual-modulus NTT、sparse/unbalanced は専用 path です。"

#: manual/design/decimal.md:79
#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:92
