msgid "[API reference](../api/decimal_gda.md) inventories the GDA value/context/outcome surface."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:189
msgid "[Tutorial](../tutorial/decimal_gda.md) demonstrates correct context threading, traps, and recovery choices."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:191
msgid "[Conformance](../conformance/decimal_gda.md) defines the pinned corpus, exclusions, and isolation checks."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:193
#, fuzzy
msgid "[`decimal` design](decimal.md) explains the separate IEEE state model and interchange boundary."
msgstr "[API](../api/decimal_gda.md)、[Tutorial](../tutorial/decimal_gda.md)、[Conformance](../conformance/decimal_gda.md)、および独立 IEEE model の [`decimal` Design](decimal.md) を参照してください。"

#: manual/design/decimal_gda_checked.md:1
msgid "`decimal_gda_checked` Design"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal_gda_checked.md:5
msgid "`GdaDecimalChecked` contains exactly one `GdaOutcome[Decimal]`. The outcome owns the current defined value, next sticky context, flags raised by the latest operation, and optional trapped signal."
msgstr "`GdaDecimalChecked` は一つの `GdaOutcome[Decimal]` だけを保持します。Outcome は current defined value、next sticky context、latest raised flags、optional trapped signal を所有します。"

#: manual/design/decimal_gda_checked.md:11
msgid "An operation on `Completed` uses its value and next context, then stores the new outcome. An operation on `Trapped` is the identity transition. This makes trap short-circuiting explicit and prevents accidental calculation past a configured control boundary."
msgstr "`Completed` 上の operation は value と next context を使い、new outcome を保存します。 `Trapped` 上の operation は identity transition です。これにより trap short-circuit が explicit になり、configured control boundary を越える計算を防ぎます。"

#: manual/design/decimal_gda_checked.md:16
msgid "Recovery Boundary"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/decimal_gda_checked.md:18
msgid "`resume_defined` is the only implicit-control escape hatch. It retains the defined value and sticky context, clears the current-step `raised` observation, and returns a completed pipeline. Binary methods accept plain GDA values so two independent sticky contexts are never merged. Traps are never converted to `ArithmeticError`."
msgstr "`resume_defined` は唯一の control escape hatch です。Defined value と sticky context を保持し、current-step `raised` observation を clear して completed pipeline に戻します。Binary method は plain GDA value を取り、独立 sticky context を merge しません。Trap を `ArithmeticError` に変換することもありません。"

#: manual/design/def.md:1
msgid "`def` Design"
msgstr "`def` 設計"

#: manual/design/def.md:5
msgid "`def` is the shared numeric vocabulary. It reexports arithmetic context/error, rounding, classification, and `BigInt` types; defines `Sign` and `PartialOrder`; and provides the deliberately small open `Floating` trait."
msgstr "共有語彙として arithmetic の context/error/rounding/classification と `BigInt` を再公開し、`Sign`、`PartialOrder`、小さな open `Floating` trait を定義します。trait は classify、sign、precision、with_precision、normalized のみを要求します。"

#: manual/design/def.md:9
msgid "Selection And Boundary"
msgstr "責務"

#: manual/design/def.md:11
#, fuzzy
msgid "`Floating` contains only representation-independent observation and retuning: `classify`, `sign`, `precision`, `with_precision`, and `normalized`. Arithmetic, ordering, parsing, context flags, and interval relations stay in narrower capability traits or concrete packages because their laws differ by domain. The helper predicates are direct pure projections over `classify`; this package contains no numerical algorithm, storage, IO, or global state."
msgstr "この package は表現をまたいで成立する観測と capability 名だけを提供し、数値 algorithm は concrete package に残します。"

#: manual/design/def.md:18
msgid "Implementing `Floating` does not imply a field, total order, IEEE format, exact arithmetic, or checked error behavior. Downstream generic code must request the additional capabilities it actually uses."
msgstr "generic code は実際に必要な arithmetic trait だけを要求し、`Floating` から rounding、error、interval semantics を推測しません。"

