msgstr "sticky context と `GdaOutcome[Decimal]`"

#: manual/getting_started.md:20
msgid "Short-circuit binary or interval pipeline"
msgstr "short-circuit binary/interval pipeline"

#: manual/getting_started.md:20
msgid "`Result[..., ArithmeticError]` retained inside a wrapper"
msgstr "wrapper 内の `Result[..., ArithmeticError]`"

#: manual/getting_started.md:21
msgid "Representation-independent comparison"
msgstr "表現に依存しない比較"

#: manual/getting_started.md:21
msgid "Exact projection, intentionally dropping metadata"
msgstr "metadata を意図的に落とす exact projection"

#: manual/getting_started.md:23
msgid "Use `numeric_expr` and `frontend/*` only when building parsers or conformance tools. `internal/*`, `consistency`, `doc_examples`, and `*_bench` are maintainer infrastructure rather than application dependencies."
msgstr "`numeric_expr` と `frontend/*` は parser や conformance tool を構築するときに使用します。`internal/*`、`consistency`、`doc_examples`、`*_bench` は maintainer infrastructure であり、application dependency ではありません。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:27
msgid "Install And Import"
msgstr "Install と import"

#: manual/getting_started.md:29
msgid "Add the current release:"
msgstr "現在の release を追加します。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:36
msgid "Import only the package boundaries used by the current MoonBit package:"
msgstr "現在の MoonBit package が必要とする package 境界だけを import します。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:50
msgid "Imports name packages, not source files. Files inside one `moon.pkg` are one compilation unit and do not create submodules."
msgstr "Import は source file ではなく package を指します。同じ `moon.pkg` 内の file は一つの compilation unit であり、個別の submodule を作りません。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:53
msgid "`Luna-Flow/arithmetic` supplies the rounding-mode type used by explicit precision and conversion boundaries. It is unnecessary when every operation uses its default rounding mode, but importing it keeps those policies visible."
msgstr "`Luna-Flow/arithmetic` は、明示的な precision 変更と変換境界で使う rounding mode の型を提供します。すべての操作で default rounding を使う場合は不要ですが、 import すると境界 policy が code 上で明示されます。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:57
msgid "Construct Values"
msgstr "値を構築する"

#: manual/getting_started.md:59
msgid "Binary coefficients are represented by `BinCoeff`; the sign is independent. Decimal parsing preserves the input quantum, including significant trailing zeros. Intervals are normally built from ordered binary endpoints."
msgstr "Binary coefficient は `BinCoeff` で表し、sign は独立です。Decimal parser は有意な末尾 zero を含む input quantum を保持します。Interval は通常、順序付けた binary endpoint から作ります。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:76
msgid "`binary` is the exact dyadic value `3 × 2^-1`; `decimal` retains exponent `-4`; and `interval` denotes every real value from 1 through 2. Call `normalized()` only when canonical cohort form is intended."
msgstr "`binary` は exact dyadic 値 `3 × 2^-1`、`decimal` は exponent `-4` を保持し、 `interval` は 1 から 2 までの全実数を表します。canonical cohort が必要な場合だけ `normalized()` を呼びます。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:80
msgid "Select A Context Model"
msgstr "Context モデルを選ぶ"

#: manual/getting_started.md:82
msgid "Use ordinary methods for unconstrained arbitrary-precision work. Use `*_ctx` when precision, exponent limits, rounding, tininess, clamp, or status flags are part of the result."
msgstr "固定 format に制約されない任意精度計算では通常 method を使います。precision、 exponent limit、rounding、tininess、clamp、status flags が結果の一部なら `*_ctx` を使います。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:95
msgid "IEEE contexts are immutable inputs and flags are explicit outputs. Combine flags when a multi-step calculation needs accumulated status. GDA instead returns the updated sticky context as part of every `GdaOutcome`."
msgstr "IEEE context は immutable input、flags は explicit output です。複数 step の accumulated status が必要なら flags を combine します。GDA は各 `GdaOutcome` に更新済み sticky context を返します。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:99
msgid "Select A Failure Model"
msgstr "失敗モデルを選ぶ"

#: manual/getting_started.md:101
msgid "The library intentionally exposes several non-equivalent failure channels:"
msgstr "Library は同一ではない複数の failure channel を意図的に公開します。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:103
msgid "`Option` is used by simple constructors where invalid input has no additional diagnostic contract."
msgstr "`Option` は追加 diagnostic contract を持たない単純 constructor 用です。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:105
msgid "`Result[T, ArithmeticError]` is used by checked scalar capabilities."
msgstr "`Result[T, ArithmeticError]` は checked scalar capability 用です。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:106
msgid "`BinaryFlags`, `DecimalFlags`, and `BallFlags` report IEEE- or domain-style conditions without replacing the returned value."
msgstr "`BinaryFlags`、`DecimalFlags`、`BallFlags` は定義済み値を生成する際の IEEE/ domain condition を報告します。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:108
msgid "`GdaOutcome[T]` always retains the GDA-defined result, even when a configured trap fires."
msgstr "`GdaOutcome[T]` は設定した trap が発火しても GDA-defined result を保持します。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:110
msgid "`DecimalChecked` accumulates IEEE flags without replacing defined NaN or infinity results; `GdaDecimalChecked` short-circuits traps while retaining their complete `GdaOutcome`."
msgstr "`DecimalChecked` は defined NaN/infinity を置き換えず IEEE flags を蓄積し、 `GdaDecimalChecked` は完全な `GdaOutcome` を保持したまま trap で短絡します。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:113
msgid "`Entire`, `Empty`, and `NaI` are interval-domain values, not generic errors."
msgstr "`Entire`、`Empty`、`NaI` は interval-domain value であり generic error ではありません。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:115
msgid "Do not convert all of these to exceptions or one universal `Result`; doing so would erase observable numerical semantics."
msgstr "これらを一つの exception や万能 `Result` に変換すると、観測可能な数値意味論が失われます。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:118
msgid "Read Results Correctly"
msgstr "結果を正しく読む"

#: manual/getting_started.md:120
msgid "Signed zero, infinity, quiet NaN, signaling NaN, and payloads may be observable on scalar representations."
msgstr "Scalar 表現は signed zero、infinity、quiet/signaling NaN、payload を保持できます。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:122
msgid "Ordinary scalar comparison is partial in the presence of NaN; total-order APIs are separate operations."
msgstr "NaN がある通常 scalar comparison は partial で、total-order API は別 operation です。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:124
msgid "`BallFloat` has containment and set relations, not a scalar total order."
msgstr "`BallFloat` には containment/set relation があり、scalar total order はありません。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:125
msgid "An interval result is correct when it encloses the mathematical result; tightness is a separate quality property."
msgstr "Interval は数学的結果を enclosure すれば正しく、tightness は別の品質です。"

#: manual/getting_started.md:127
msgid "`SemanticScalar` compares mathematical meaning but intentionally loses precision, quantum, signed zero, NaN payloads, decorations, and flags."
msgstr "`SemanticScalar` は数学的意味を比較しますが、precision、quantum、signed zero、 NaN payload、decoration、flags を意図的に失います。"

