#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:3
#, fuzzy
msgid "Use `bin_float` when values are naturally dyadic, when precision must exceed a host `Float`/`Double`, or when binary16/32/64/128 rounding and status are part of the result. This tutorial targets `floating` 0.8.0; see [API](../api/bin_float.md) for the complete inventory and [Conformance](../conformance/bin_float.md) for the verified IEEE boundary."
msgstr "自然な dyadic、host Float/Double を超える precision、または binary16/32/64/128 の rounding/status が contract の場合に使用します。0.8.0 対応です。"

